    Body of the `useragreement.php` page, rendered into a chrome-less
    HTML envelope by `App\Http\Controllers\Legacy\UserAgreementController`.

    Phase 2 of the legacy migration. The original `public/useragreement.php`
    interleaved `<?php echo $SITENAME ?>` / `<?php echo $BASEURL ?>` /
    `<?php echo $baseUrl ?>` (= `getSchemeAndHttpHost()`) directly into
    a static legal text and rendered it inside `stdhead` / `begin_main_frame`
    / `begin_frame` / `end_frame` / `end_main_frame` / `stdfoot` chrome.

    The Blade view receives the same three values:
      - `$sitename`     — `basic.SITENAME` setting (hostname-style label).
      - `$baseurl`      — `basic.BASEURL` setting (hostname without scheme),
                          matching the legacy `$BASEURL` from `include/config.php`.
      - `$baseurlFull`  — `Request::getSchemeAndHttpHost()`, matching the
                          legacy `$baseUrl = getSchemeAndHttpHost()`.

    The body is identical to the legacy text. Output escaping is handled
    by Blade `{{ }}` autoescaping — the legacy script emitted these
    values raw, which was a latent XSS sink if `basic.SITENAME` or
    `basic.BASEURL` ever contained `<script>` or markup. The Phase 2
    rewrite closes that gap as a side effect of moving rendering into
    Blade.
